{ [%anno "jomega", jomega] Prerequisites
-
Readers of this study should have the book "Chess Structures: A Grandmaster Guide", Mauricio Flores Rios, Quality Chess, First Edition 2015.

The corresponding chapter introductions in the book have White's plans and Black's plans for each structure.

The reader should either already have a good grasp of chess terminology and chess ideas, and the basics of chess openings, or is willing to learn what is necessary. For example, the material covered in "The Complete Book of Chess Strategy", by Jeremy Silman.

This book by Silman is a good reference book for openings, chess terminology and chess ideas. Silman gives the ideas behind selected openings in the first part of the book, while the second part of the book is a glossary of chess ideas. }
 *


